
                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 1       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


    1                                   ; YMXR.S - the player: a tune's rows to the YM2149 and the MFP, one row a
    2                                   ; frame, and a source's rows to one register at a timer's rate.
    3                                   ;
    4                                   ; doc/SPEC.md is the contract: section 4 is YMXR_play and section 5 the
    5                                   ; tick handlers. What this player takes is the bound tune of
    6                                   ; doc/BINARIES.md: the tune file's tables, and no code, bound by a tool
    7                                   ; with the image DTX packaged the table with. The player calls that
    8                                   ; image's slots (DTX, doc/abi.md) and reads the row they give.
    9                                   ;
   10                                   ; The calls, by the jump table at the top of the binary:
   11                                   ;
   12                                   ;   YMXR_init   a0 the bound tune, on an even address; a1 the workspace,
   13                                   ;               on a long. d0 is 0, or -1 for one this player does not
   14                                   ;               read.
   15                                   ;   YMXR_play   a0 the workspace. One row. d0 is 0, or -1 where the tune
   16                                   ;               has played its last row and does not repeat: nothing is
   17                                   ;               written then.
   18                                   ;   YMXR_stop   a0 the workspace. The claimed timers stopped, disabled and
   19                                   ;               masked; the three volumes silenced.
   20                                   ;
   21                                   ; Every call clobbers d0-d5 and a0-a5 and leaves d6, d7 and a6 as they
   22                                   ; were. YMXR_play runs in supervisor mode, at any interrupt level: every
   23                                   ; write of a select and a value is one movep, which no tick lands inside.
   24                                   ;
   25                                   ; A call writes the row the call before it took, and takes the next when
   26                                   ; its writes are made: the row's writes then leave a host's clock at one
   27                                   ; offset, where an advance before them would move by what the refill of
   28                                   ; the row costs. Init takes the first row.
   29                                   ;
   30                                   ; The workspace is YMXR_FIXED bytes, then the state block the image's
   31                                   ; format block asks for, which the bound tune states at offset 12
   32                                   ; (BINARIES.md): a host allocates YMXR_FIXED plus that.
   33                                   ;
   34                                   ; The host owns the machine. This player saves and restores no vector, no
   35                                   ; timer control and no interrupt enable: around init and stop a host keeps
   36                                   ; what it needs of the vectors at $134, $120, $114 and $110, of TACR, TBCR
   37                                   ; and both nibbles of TCDCR, and of bits 5 and 0 of IERA and IMRA and bits
   38                                   ; 5 and 4 of IERB and IMRB. A timer an effect does not run is never
   39                                   ; touched. The MFP is taken in software end-of-interrupt mode, as TOS
   40                                   ; leaves it, and the vectors are the 68000's at zero.
   41                                   ;
   42                                   ; The player patches itself: the row's displacements and the branches
   43                                   ; over the effects the tune does not run at init, and the tick handlers'
   44                                   ; operands at every start. It runs from RAM, and one loaded copy serves
   45                                   ; one workspace.
   46                                   ;
   47                                   ; YMXR_PERF equ 1 assembles the raster monitor in: the play call paints
   48                                   ; the background red for as long as its work runs, one scanline to 512
   49                                   ; cycles, and each tick handler paints its own colour where the beam
   50                                   ; stands. A tick's band is a few hundred cycles wide and hard to read,
   51                                   ; so each handler adds a count of what its own instructions cost, which
   52                                   ; the next call burns off as a yellow bar after its own work, the
   53                                   ; register writes among them: the bar shows what the handlers cost the
   54                                   ; frame, and no chip write moves for the bar. What a tick costs beyond
   55                                   ; its handler, the 44 cycles the 68000 spends entering an interrupt and
   56                                   ; the 20 on the rte, stands where the tick landed and is not counted


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 2       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


   57                                   ; here. The call waits for the display to start before it paints, since
   58                                   ; the VBL fires far above the screen and an unsynced bar lands in the
   59                                   ; top border; the wait stands before the red mark, so it costs the
   60                                   ; figures nothing. Each count is an estimate, in turns of ten cycles,
   61                                   ; and the monitor is for reading a run: with the switch off, the
   62                                   ; default, no byte and no cycle of it stands.
   63                                   
   64           =594D5842               YMXR_MAGIC      equ     $594D5842       ; YMXB, the bound tune
   65           =00000001               YMXR_VERSION    equ     $0001           ; its version
   66           =0000001E               YMXR_COLUMNS    equ     30
   67           =00000012               YMXR_SITES      equ     18              ; the other read sites (ymxr_sites)
   68                                   
   69                                   ; The raster monitor, off unless the assembly defines it (rmac
   70                                   ; -dYMXR_PERF=1).
   71                                                   .if     ^^defined YMXR_PERF
   72                                 -                 .else
   73           =00000000               YMXR_PERF       equ     0
   74                                                   .endif
   75           =00001F40               PERF_SYNC       equ     8000            ; the wait's ceiling, over a frame
   76                                                                           ; of turns, so a call from
   77                                                                           ; anywhere runs on
   78           =00000700               PERF_FRAME      equ     $700            ; the call's own work
   79           =00000770               PERF_BAR        equ     $770            ; the timers' burnt bar
   80           =FFFF8240               PERF_COLOUR     equ     $FFFF8240       ; the background
   81           =FFFF8209               PERF_BEAM       equ     $FFFF8209       ; the video address counter's low
   82                                                                           ; byte, which moves while the chip
   83                                                                           ; fetches pixels
   84                                   ; What a tick of each kind is counted at, in turns of ten cycles, beside
   85                                   ; what performance.md measures each at: a row written 108 cycles, the
   86                                   ; marker with the place to row RR 130, the marker with the timer stopped
   87                                   ; 116. Each count stands within a twentieth of its measurement, and
   88                                   ; PlayerTest holds the three to the document's figures.
   89           =0000000B               PERF_ON         equ     11
   90           =0000000D               PERF_LOOP       equ     13
   91           =0000000C               PERF_STOP       equ     12
   92                                   
   93                                   ; The bound tune (BINARIES.md).
   94           =00000004               TF_VERSION      equ     4
   95           =00000006               TF_RATE         equ     6
   96           =00000008               TF_EFFECTS      equ     8
   97           =00000009               TF_SOURCES      equ     9
   98           =0000000C               TF_STATE        equ     12
   99           =00000010               TF_IMAGE        equ     16
  100           =00000014               TF_INDEX        equ     20
  101                                   
  102                                   ; The image's format block (DTX, abi.md 1), and its slots.
  103           =00000010               IM_FORMAT       equ     16
  104           =00000013               IM_VARIANT      equ     19
  105           =00000000               IM_INIT         equ     0
  106           =00000004               IM_METADATA     equ     4
  107           =0000000C               IM_ADVANCE      equ     12
  108                                   
  109                                   ; A DTX1 table's header, and where a source's rows begin (DTX, SPEC.md 1).
  110           =00000004               DT_ROWS         equ     4
  111           =0000000A               DT_REPEAT       equ     10
  112           =00000010               DT_PAYLOAD      equ     16


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 3       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


  113                                   
  114                                   ; The workspace.
  115           =00000000               WS_TUNE         equ     0               ; the bound tune
  116           =00000004               WS_IMAGE        equ     4               ; the image in it
  117           =00000008               WS_ROWS         equ     8               ; rows to the last, or to the wrap
  118           =0000000C               WS_R            equ     12
  119           =00000010               WS_RR           equ     16
  120           =00000014               WS_EFFECTS      equ     20              ; a byte: the effects the tune runs
  121           =00000018               WS_FX           equ     24              ; four effects, FX_SIZE each
  122           =00000000               FX_TARGET       equ     0               ; the target the player holds
  123           =00000001               FX_SELECT       equ     1               ; the select it last took
  124           =00000002               FX_COUNT        equ     2               ; the count it last took
  125           =00000004               FX_FIRST        equ     4               ; the running source's first row
  126           =00000008               FX_SIZE         equ     8
  127           =00000038               WS_ROW          equ     56              ; the row the next call writes
  128           =0000003C               YMXR_FIXED      equ     60
  129           =0000003C               WS_STATE        equ     60              ; the image's state block, on a long
  130                                   
  131                                   ; The chip.
  132           =FFFF8800               YM_SELECT       equ     $FFFF8800
  133           =000000C0               YM_PORTS        equ     $C0             ; R7's port directions, the ST's
  134                                   
  135                                   ; The MFP: the timers by effect (SPEC.md 2.3).
  136                                   ;                       control   data      vector  IER     bit  keep  shift
  137                                   ; effect 0, Timer A     $FFFA19   $FFFA1F   $134    $FFFA07 5    $F0   0
  138                                   ; effect 1, Timer D     $FFFA1D   $FFFA25   $110    $FFFA09 4    $F0   0
  139                                   ; effect 2, Timer B     $FFFA1B   $FFFA21   $120    $FFFA07 0    $F0   0
  140                                   ; effect 3, Timer C     $FFFA1D   $FFFA23   $114    $FFFA09 5    $0F   4
  141                                   ; IER+4 is the pending register, IER+8 the in-service, IER+12 the mask.
  142                                   
  143                                   ; A tick handler's operands, patched at a start, stand at fixed offsets
  144                                   ; into it; the equates are below the handlers, since the raster monitor's
  145                                   ; marks stand between the three blocks a handler is made of and the
  146                                   ; assembler measures the distances.
  147                                   
  148                                   ; ---------------------------------------------------------------- macros
  149                                   
  150                                   ; A column into d1, or into d2. The displacement is i strides, patched at
  151                                   ; init: rmac would fold a zero away, so a placeholder stands here.
  152                                                   .macro  READ    col
  153                                 . c\{col}:
  154                                 .                 move.b  $7FFF(a1),d1
  155                                 .                 .endm
  156                                   
  157                                                   .macro  READ2   col
  158                                 . c\{col}:
  159                                 .                 move.b  $7FFF(a1),d2
  160                                 .                 .endm
  161                                   
  162                                   ; A second read of a column, or a column ored into d1, at a site of its
  163                                   ; own that init patches from the table of sites (ymxr_sites).
  164                                                   .macro  QREAD   col
  165                                 . q\{col}:
  166                                 .                 move.b  $7FFF(a1),d1
  167                                 .                 .endm
  168                                   


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 4       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


  169                                                   .macro  QOR     col
  170                                 . q\{col}:
  171                                 .                 or.b    $7FFF(a1),d1
  172                                 .                 .endm
  173                                   
  174                                   ; A column that fills its byte, on the row where the column beside it is
  175                                   ; 0: written where it is not 0, and nothing else to test.
  176                                                   .macro  PLAIN   col,select
  177                                 .                 QREAD   \col
  178                                 .                 beq.s   .no\~
  179                                 .                 move.w  #\select,d0
  180                                 .                 move.b  d1,d0
  181                                 .                 movep.w d0,(a2)
  182                                 . .no\~:
  183                                 .                 .endm
  184                                   
  185                                   ; A column with a set bit, to its register: the column read, and where
  186                                   ; it is set the select put above it and one movep for the pair.
  187                                                   .macro  WRITE   col,select
  188                                 .                 READ    \col
  189                                 .                 bpl.s   .no\~
  190                                 .                 move.w  #\select,d0
  191                                 .                 move.b  d1,d0
  192                                 .                 movep.w d0,(a2)
  193                                 . .no\~:
  194                                 .                 .endm
  195                                   
  196                                   ; A column that fills its byte, reserving 0: written where it is not 0,
  197                                   ; or where the bit beside it, in d2, says 0 is the value.
  198                                                   .macro  RESERVED col,bit,select
  199                                 .                 READ    \col
  200                                 .                 bne.s   .go\~
  201                                 .                 btst    #\bit,d2
  202                                 .                 beq.s   .no\~
  203                                 . .go\~:          move.w  #\select,d0
  204                                 .                 move.b  d1,d0
  205                                 .                 movep.w d0,(a2)
  206                                 . .no\~:
  207                                 .                 .endm
  208                                   
  209                                   ; A tone period: the coarse column into d2, for its bit 6 and its own
  210                                   ; value, then the fine column against it.
  211                                                   .macro  TONE    fine,coarse,fsel,csel
  212                                 .                 READ2   \coarse
  213                                 .                 READ    \fine
  214                                 .                 bne.s   .go\~
  215                                 .                 tst.b   d2                      ; a coarse column of 0 has no
  216                                 .                 beq.s   .nc\~                   ; set bit and no bit beside
  217                                 .                 btst    #6,d2
  218                                 .                 beq.s   .nf\~
  219                                 . .go\~:          move.w  #\fsel,d0
  220                                 .                 move.b  d1,d0
  221                                 .                 movep.w d0,(a2)
  222                                 . .nf\~:          tst.b   d2
  223                                 .                 bpl.s   .nc\~
  224                                 .                 move.w  #\csel,d1


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 5       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


  225                                 .                 move.b  d2,d1
  226                                 .                 movep.w d1,(a2)
  227                                 . .nc\~:
  228                                 .                 .endm
  229                                   
  230                                   ; One effect: the target kept, the source started or stopped, the timer's
  231                                   ; count and select written, with the timer's and the place's reset.
  232                                                   .macro  EFFECT  fx,ct,cs,cc,cn,ctrl,data,ier,bit,keep,shift,shared,tick
  233                                 . \{tick}_over:
  234                                 .                 bra.w   \{tick}_done             ; two nops where the tune
  235                                 .                 QREAD   \ct                     ; runs this effect (init)
  236                                 .                 QOR     \cs                     ; the three set bits at once
  237                                 .                 QOR     \cc
  238                                 .                 bmi.s   \{tick}_some
  239                                 .                 QREAD   \cn                     ; the count alone, or nothing
  240                                 .                 beq.w   \{tick}_done
  241                                 .                 move.b  d1,\data.w              ; the count, the timer running on
  242                                 .                 move.b  d1,\fx+FX_COUNT(a6)
  243                                 .                 bra.w   \{tick}_done
  244                                 . \{tick}_some:
  245                                 .                 READ2   \cc
  246                                 .                 tst.b   d2                      ; the timer's reset stops the
  247                                 .                 bpl.s   .kept\~                 ; timer before the source is
  248                                 .                 btst    #6,d2                   ; switched, so no tick of the
  249                                 .                 beq.s   .kept\~                 ; old rate takes the new
  250                                 .                 andi.b  #\keep,\ctrl.w          ; source, and the tick latched
  251                                 .                 bclr    #\bit,(\ier+4).w        ; before the stop is dropped
  252                                 . .kept\~:
  253                                 .                 READ    \ct
  254                                 .                 bpl.s   .t\~
  255                                 .                 and.b   #$7F,d1
  256                                 .                 move.b  d1,\fx+FX_TARGET(a6)
  257                                 . .t\~:           READ    \cs
  258                                 .                 bpl.s   .rate\~
  259                                 .                 and.w   #$7F,d1
  260                                 .                 beq.s   .stop\~
  261                                 . ; a start: the source's rows through the index, the handler aimed at them
  262                                 .                 movea.l WS_TUNE(a6),a3
  263                                 .                 lsl.w   #2,d1
  264                                 .                 move.l  TF_INDEX-4(a3,d1.w),d0
  265                                 .                 adda.l  d0,a3                   ; the source's DTX1 table
  266                                 .                 lea     DT_PAYLOAD(a3),a4       ; its first row
  267                                 .                 move.l  DT_REPEAT(a3),d0        ; the loop cell: row RR, or 0
  268                                 .                 cmp.l   DT_ROWS(a3),d0          ; where the source plays once
  269                                 .                 beq.s   .once\~
  270                                 .                 add.l   a4,d0
  271                                 .                 bra.s   .aim\~
  272                                 . .once\~:        moveq   #0,d0
  273                                 . ; the handler's three operands stand under one mask, since the timer may
  274                                 . ; run: a tick between the target register and the place writes the old
  275                                 . ; source's row to the new target, and one between the place and the loop
  276                                 . ; cell takes the new place against the cell the old source left
  277                                 . .aim\~:         lea     \tick(pc),a5
  278                                 . ; The three behind level 7, so a tick takes none of them half made. The
  279                                 . ; window is three writes wide and costs no measurable jitter: the ticks
  280                                 . ; of a tune running one effect keep their period to 0.31 per cent with


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 6       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


  281                                 . ; it and to 0.31 without, where the reference player's keep 0.33. The
  282                                 . ; place the row does not reset is read in the window too, since a tick
  283                                 . ; between the read and the write steps it (1.9).
  284                                 .                 move.w  sr,-(sp)
  285                                 .                 ori.w   #$0700,sr
  286                                 .                 move.b  \fx+FX_TARGET(a6),TICK_SEL(a5)
  287                                 .                 move.l  a4,d1                   ; the place: the first row,
  288                                 .                 btst    #5,d2                   ; or the row it stands on in
  289                                 .                 bne.s   .put\~                  ; the rows it replaces
  290                                 .                 add.l   TICK_PTR(a5),d1
  291                                 .                 sub.l   \fx+FX_FIRST(a6),d1
  292                                 . .put\~:         move.l  d1,TICK_PTR(a5)
  293                                 .                 move.l  d0,TICK_CELL(a5)
  294                                 .                 move.w  (sp)+,sr
  295                                 .                 move.l  a4,\fx+FX_FIRST(a6)
  296                                 . ; the start placed the source, so the row's place reset is made: a tick
  297                                 . ; before the select steps the place on, and the reset below would undo it
  298                                 .                 bclr    #5,d2
  299                                 .                 bra.s   .rate\~
  300                                 . .stop\~:        andi.b  #\keep,\ctrl.w      ; select 0: the timer stops
  301                                 .                 bclr    #\bit,(\ier+4).w    ; and drops its latched tick
  302                                 . .rate\~:        READ    \cn
  303                                 .                 tst.b   d2
  304                                 .                 bpl.s   .live\~
  305                                 .                 btst    #6,d2
  306                                 .                 beq.s   .set\~
  307                                 . ; the timer's reset: stopped above, the count, then the select
  308                                 .                 tst.b   d1
  309                                 .                 bne.s   .cnt\~
  310                                 .                 move.b  \fx+FX_COUNT(a6),d1
  311                                 . .cnt\~:         move.b  d1,\data.w
  312                                 .                 move.b  d1,\fx+FX_COUNT(a6)
  313                                 .                 bra.s   .sel\~
  314                                 . .live\~:        tst.b   d1
  315                                 .                 beq.s   .done\~
  316                                 .                 move.b  d1,\data.w            ; the count, the timer running on
  317                                 .                 move.b  d1,\fx+FX_COUNT(a6)
  318                                 .                 bra.s   .done\~
  319                                 . .set\~:         tst.b   d1
  320                                 .                 beq.s   .sel\~
  321                                 .                 move.b  d1,\data.w
  322                                 .                 move.b  d1,\fx+FX_COUNT(a6)
  323                                 . .sel\~:         move.b  d2,d1
  324                                 .                 and.b   #7,d1
  325                                 .                 move.b  d1,\fx+FX_SELECT(a6)
  326                                 .                 .if     \shift
  327                                 .                 lsl.b   #\shift,d1
  328                                 .                 .endif
  329                                 . ; the control register takes one write: a select written to a running
  330                                 . ; timer neither stops nor reloads the running count (SPEC.md 1.9), and
  331                                 . ; select 0 in front of the new select stops the timer and costs it the
  332                                 . ; prescaler's partial count. Timer A's and Timer B's control register is
  333                                 . ; the timer's own, so one move writes it and no interrupt can fall
  334                                 . ; inside an instruction; Timers C and D share theirs, and only there
  335                                 . ; does the read, the mask and the or run at level 7.
  336                                 .                 .if     \shared


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 7       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


  337                                 .                 move.w  sr,-(sp)
  338                                 .                 ori.w   #$0700,sr
  339                                 .                 move.b  \ctrl.w,d0
  340                                 .                 and.b   #\keep,d0
  341                                 .                 or.b    d1,d0
  342                                 .                 move.b  d0,\ctrl.w
  343                                 .                 move.w  (sp)+,sr
  344                                 .                 .else
  345                                 .                 move.b  d1,\ctrl.w
  346                                 .                 .endif
  347                                 .                 btst    #5,d2
  348                                 .                 beq.s   .done\~
  349                                 .                 lea     \tick(pc),a5          ; the place's reset
  350                                 .                 move.l  \fx+FX_FIRST(a6),TICK_PTR(a5)
  351                                 . .done\~:
  352                                 . \{tick}_done:
  353                                 .                 .endm
  354                                   
  355                                   ; The branch over an effect's columns made two nops where the tune runs
  356                                   ; the effect.
  357                                                   .macro  RUNS    i,over
  358                                 .                 btst    #\i,WS_EFFECTS(a6)
  359                                 .                 beq.s   .no\~
  360                                 .                 lea     \over(pc),a3
  361                                 .                 move.l  #$4E714E71,(a3)
  362                                 . .no\~:
  363                                 .                 .endm
  364                                   
  365                                   ; One timer claimed, where the tune runs its effect: stopped, aimed at
  366                                   ; its handler, enabled and unmasked.
  367                                                   .macro  CLAIM   i,ctrl,keep,vector,ier,bit,tick
  368                                 .                 btst    #\i,WS_EFFECTS(a6)
  369                                 .                 beq.s   .no\~
  370                                 .                 andi.b  #\keep,\ctrl.w
  371                                 .                 lea     \tick(pc),a3
  372                                 .                 move.l  a3,\vector.w
  373                                 .                 bclr    #\bit,(\ier+4).w
  374                                 .                 bset    #\bit,\ier.w
  375                                 .                 bset    #\bit,(\ier+12).w
  376                                 . .no\~:
  377                                 .                 .endm
  378                                   
  379                                   ; One timer handed back: stopped, disabled, masked, its pending dropped.
  380                                                   .macro  RELEASE i,ctrl,keep,ier,bit
  381                                 .                 btst    #\i,WS_EFFECTS(a6)
  382                                 .                 beq.s   .no\~
  383                                 .                 andi.b  #\keep,\ctrl.w
  384                                 .                 bclr    #\bit,\ier.w
  385                                 .                 bclr    #\bit,(\ier+12).w
  386                                 .                 bclr    #\bit,(\ier+4).w
  387                                 . .no\~:
  388                                 .                 .endm
  389                                   
  390                                   ; The monitor's mark: the background kept on the stack and this handler's
  391                                   ; colour written.
  392                                                   .macro  MARK    colour


                                        /Users/rapido/git/YMXR/68k/YMXR.S Page 8       11:37:16 pm 7-Sep-2026        RMAC 2.4.03 (Linux/OSX)


  393                                 .                 .if     YMXR_PERF
  394                                 .                 move.w  PERF_COLOUR.w,-(sp)
  395                                 .                 move.w  #\colour,PERF_COLOUR.w
  396                                 .                 .endif
  397                                 .                 .endm
  398                                   
  399                                   ; The other end of a mark: this tick's estimated cost counted, in turns
  400                                   ; of ten cycles, and the background put back. It stands after the write
  401                                   ; the tick makes and before the end of interrupt, so a nested tick of a
  402                                   ; higher timer marks and unmarks inside it.
  403                                                   .macro  COUNT   turns
  404                                 .                 .if     YMXR_PERF
  405                                 .                 move.l  a0,-(sp)
  406                                 .                 lea     ymxr_perf_acc(pc),a0
  407                                 .                 add.w   #\turns,(a0)
  408                                 .                 movea.l (sp)+,a0
  409                                 .                 move.w  (sp)+,PERF_COLOUR.w
  410                                 .                 .endif
  411                                 .                 .endm
  412                                   
  413                                   ; A tick (SPEC.md 5): the place's row to the target, the place advanced;
  414                                   ; on the marker, the place to row RR, or the timer stopped. No register
  415                                   ; is used: the place is the write's own operand, stepped in place. The
  416                                   ; interrupt level drops once the select and the value are written, so a
  417                                   ; higher timer may nest, and the in-service bit is cleared by hand, as
  418                                   ; software end-of-interrupt mode asks.
  419                                                   .macro  TICK    name,eoi,eoir,ctrl,keep,colour
  420                                 . \name:
  421                                 .                 MARK    \colour
  422                                 . \{name}_row:    move.b  #8,YM_SELECT.w          ; +3: the target register
  423                                 .                 move.b  ($12345678).l,YM_SELECT+2.w ; +8: the place
  424                                 .                 bmi.s   .last\~
  425                                 .                 move.w  #$2500,sr
  426                                 .                 addq.l  #1,($12345678).l        ; +22: the place, stepped
  427                                 .                 COUNT   PERF_ON
  428                                 .                 move.b  #\eoi,\eoir.w
  429                                 .                 rte
  430                                 . .last\~:
  431                                 . \{name}_mark:   tst.l   ($12345678).l           ; +2: the loop cell
  432                                 .                 beq.s   .stop\~
  433                                 .                 move.l  ($12345678).l,($12345678).l ; +10 the cell, +14 the place
  434                                 .                 COUNT   PERF_LOOP
  435                                 .                 move.b  #\eoi,\eoir.w
  436                                 .                 rte
  437                                 . .stop\~:        andi.b  #\keep,\ctrl.w
  438                                 .                 COUNT   PERF_STOP
  439                                 .                 move.b  #\eoi,\eoir.w
  440                                 .                 rte
  441                                 . \{name}_cell:   dc.l    0                       ; the loop cell
  442                                 .                 .endm
  443                                   
